{"key":"VideoWindow","text":"## VideoWindow\n\nThe **Video Window** plays one recording from the Gallery. Click a video tile\nin the Gallery and it opens here; several videos can be open at once, each in\nits own window.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nVideo | 0.50, 0.42 | The picture. In a browser this is the native video player with its own controls; in the Editor click the picture to play or pause and drag the bar underneath to seek.\nControls Bar | 0.50, 0.90 | Loop pill (green when on), the Speed slider with its live readout, and the volume slider.\n\n---\n\n### Playback\n\n- **Loop** — repeats the video; remembered per video\n- **Speed** — from -2 to 5. Zero reads Pause; negative values play backwards by stepping, which is choppy outside the browser\n- **Vol** — volume from silent to full\n- **Right-click the picture** — *Set as Thumbnail* saves the current frame as the Gallery poster for this video\n\n### Title bar\n\n- **Double-click the title** — rename the video in place; the file and its poster are renamed on GitHub and the Gallery tile updates\n- **Right-click the title** — Rename, or Delete from GitHub (asks first, then removes the file and its poster and closes the window)\n\n### Formats\n\n- Use **.mp4** (H.264/AAC); it plays in every browser, on mobile and in the Editor\n- **.webm** plays in Chrome, Firefox and Android only; **.mov** in Safari only\n\n### Shortcuts\n\n- None; the controls are on screen.\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: OS\n\n---","screenshot":""}